WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.279 --> 00:00:04.079
Big milestone for the David Pakman show achieved yesterday. We reached

00:00:05.890 --> 00:00:07.390
500,000 subscribers

00:00:07.390 --> 00:00:14.429
on our YouTube channel youtube.com/thedavidpakmanshow. And what I like to do whenever we reach a big milestone on the YouTube

00:00:14.429 --> 00:00:19.679
channel is look back at old analytics; and I went back and looked at the first month we were on YouTube..

00:00:19.869 --> 00:00:23.039
Okay, Pat was in kindergarten at the time... We had

00:00:23.980 --> 00:00:29.670
721 views that month. Okay,I didn't mean to miss speak. I'm not saying we had 721 viewers,

00:00:29.670 --> 00:00:35.069
I'm not saying we had 721 views per day. The first month

00:00:35.070 --> 00:00:38.729
we were on YouTube, the entire month we ended up with

00:00:39.910 --> 00:00:42.299
721 views and four subscribers,

00:00:43.030 --> 00:00:45.030
three of which were probably

00:00:45.160 --> 00:00:50.879
accounts my mom made. Okay, those are the right numbers. In July of 2018, last month

00:00:51.640 --> 00:00:53.500
we added

00:00:53.500 --> 00:00:59.669
16,000 subscribers. We had 16,000 new subscribers just last July and more than 8.1

00:01:00.070 --> 00:01:02.489
million views and it happened

00:01:03.010 --> 00:01:05.010
rolling over from

00:01:05.860 --> 00:01:08.159
499 thousand 999

00:01:08.979 --> 00:01:11.368
subscribers to the miraculous

00:01:12.159 --> 00:01:13.990
majestic and

00:01:13.990 --> 00:01:15.990
towering number of

00:01:17.680 --> 00:01:19.820
500,000 views. I was sitting there watching it,

00:01:19.820 --> 00:01:24.689
Pat was sitting there watching it and it was a moment to behold and

00:01:24.850 --> 00:01:26.220
This is huge for us

00:01:26.220 --> 00:01:29.009
Thanks to everyone of the 500 thousand. Now

00:01:29.009 --> 00:01:33.959
it's even more  - we're already up to like 500,150  or something like that

00:01:34.030 --> 00:01:41.099
so onward and upward to 1 million; more content, more miniseries, more long-form pieces, interviews everything. But I do want to say -

00:01:41.920 --> 00:01:43.920
It's really not the subscribers that matter

00:01:43.930 --> 00:01:46.049
It's the views. You could have a million subscribers

00:01:46.479 --> 00:01:52.109
and no views and that's where our focus continues to be. People may not know this but of

00:01:52.390 --> 00:01:59.729
our views only 30% come from subscribers; 70% of our entire channel views are from non

00:02:00.159 --> 00:02:06.298
subscribers who either see our video recommended when watching something else or make a search for something like

00:02:06.670 --> 00:02:12.390
"Trump embarrasses himself hugely in front of the Japanese Prime Minister" and maybe our video comes up

00:02:12.390 --> 00:02:17.960
So subscriber milestone -very important, but onward and upward and continuing.

00:02:17.960 --> 00:02:21.199
Pat: Yeah, our channel is ranked 6000 in video views

00:02:21.420 --> 00:02:23.040
Which doesn't sound that impressive

00:02:23.040 --> 00:02:27.919
until you compare it to like the tens of millions of YouTube channels out there and then it sounds pretty good.

00:02:27.920 --> 00:02:33.050
David: And then if you watch on TV or listen on the radio or to the podcast then this has nothing to do with any of

00:02:33.050 --> 00:02:34.670
your experience with the show

00:02:34.670 --> 00:02:37.430
So in that sense if you're not a YouTube viewer

00:02:37.430 --> 00:02:43.879
I apologize for the interruption and we're gonna take a quick break and then get back to the meat of the programming

00:02:43.880 --> 00:02:47.419
But if you are part of our success on YouTube, thank you. I really do appreciate it.

00:02:47.760 --> 00:02:51.139
Send your messages of congratulations or of trolling and

00:02:51.720 --> 00:02:54.350
predictions that this is almost the end for the show,

00:02:54.350 --> 00:02:59.689
